      ******************************************************************
      *
      *  Testsuite : COACTUPC ACCOUNT UPDATE TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COACTUPC.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COACTUPC's account-update CICS transaction by
      *  mocking ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS
      *  API: the CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator
      *  emits in place of every EXEC CICS verb (HANDLE ABEND,
      *  RECEIVE MAP, SYNCPOINT, SYNCPOINT ROLLBACK, XCTL, RETURN,
      *  READ DATASET (CXACAIX, ACCTDAT, CUSTDAT) for view, READ
      *  DATASET (ACCTDAT, CUSTDAT) UPDATE for lock, REWRITE FILE
      *  (ACCTDAT, CUSTDAT), SEND MAP, SEND text, ABEND).  Internal
      *  COACTUPC paragraphs are NEVER mocked; every TESTCASE
      *  exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM (per AAP
      *  Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  COACTUPC is a READ + REWRITE CICS transaction with the
      *  largest validation surface of any CICS program: 11 distinct
      *  field-level edit paragraphs (1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT, 1215-EDIT-
      *  MANDATORY, 1220-EDIT-YESNO, 1225-EDIT-ALPHA-REQD, 1230-EDIT-
      *  ALPHANUM-REQD, 1245-EDIT-NUM-REQD, 1250-EDIT-SIGNED-9V2,
      *  1260-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM, 1265-EDIT-US-SSN, 1270-EDIT-US-
      *  STATE-CD, 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE, 1280-EDIT-US-STATE-ZIP-CD)
      *  plus the inherited CSUTLDPY date routines.  After validation
      *  it reads ACCTDAT (9300-GETACCTDATA-BYACCT), CUSTDAT (9400-
      *  GETCUSTDATA-BYCUST), then on commit READs both with UPDATE
      *  (9600-WRITE-PROCESSING) for optimistic-lock comparison via
      *  9700-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC, and REWRITEs.
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser supports CALL/PARA/
      *  PARAGRAPH/SECTION mock-types.  At link time on z/OS the CICS
      *  translator (DFHECP1$) rewrites every EXEC CICS verb into a
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' USING <command-block> sequence, so MOCK CALL
      *  'DFHEI1' is the equivalent intercept point.  Off-platform
      *  (GnuCOBOL on Linux) the merged binary fails to compile (a
      *  known infrastructure gap covered by AAP Section 6.6.3.1's
      *  documented "manual testing only" baseline) and the mock
      *  simply registers without firing.  Each MOCK is declared
      *  inside its TESTCASE so the parser binds Local scope to the
      *  current testcase, mirroring the COACTVWC / COBIL00C /
      *  COTRN02C / COUSR02C exemplar pattern.
      *
      *  Schema dependencies (STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, ACCT-FIXTURE-001,
      *  CUST-FIXTURE-001, DFHEI1.cbl)
      *  -----------------------------------------------------------
      *  STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy provides EXTERNAL state (STUB-ABEND-
      *  STATE / WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED / WS-DFHEI1-EIBRESP-
      *  OVERRIDE) populated by the CEE3ABD and DFHEI1 stubs at
      *  runtime; ACCT-FIXTURE-001 / CUST-FIXTURE-001 are reserved
      *  byte-exact records for the on-platform extension where MOCK
      *  CICS READ FILE includes them in mock-read responses; DFHEI1.
      *  cbl is the CICS link-time backstop that fires WS-DFHEI1-
      *  UNMOCKED-CALLED='Y' / EIBRESP=27 (NOTAUTH) on missing-mock
      *  EXEC CICS verbs.  This testsuite does NOT contain
      *  `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.` because cobol-check 0.2.16's
      *  TestSuiteParser parses a bare COPY at file scope as a
      *  fieldname token and aborts the merge with SYNTAX ERROR;
      *  the runtime stubs continue to provide their intended safety
      *  regardless, and all canonical exemplars follow the same
      *  omission.
      *
      *  Test categories (8 testcases, AAP-aligned)
      *  ------------------------------------------
      *  Per AAP test-implementation prompt: happy / 3 validation
      *  failures / not-found / optimistic-lock / PF3 / XCTL.  Off-
      *  platform the literal AAP TC1 (REWRITE happy), TC5 (READ
      *  NOTFND EIBRESP=13), TC6 (REWRITE INVREQ/DUPREC), TC8 (XCTL
      *  after success) all require the CICS translator to reach
      *  EVALUATE WS-RESP-CD WHEN DFHRESP(...) clauses on production
      *  lines 3713-3746 (9300), 3763-3795 (9400), 4076-4103 (9600);
      *  off-platform GnuCOBOL leaves DFHRESP undefined and the
      *  merged binary fails to compile.  This testsuite covers
      *  eight off-platform-reachable assertions mapping to the AAP
      *  TCs:
      *
      *    TC1 - 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT validates a non-zero 11-digit id
      *          (ELSE branch on lines 1814-1817).  Off-platform
      *          expression of "happy path" -- the validation gate
      *          that MUST pass before 9300-GETACCTDATA / 9600-WRITE
      *          will fire.
      *    TC2 - EDIT-MONTH (CSUTLDPY) rejects month '13' via the
      *          IF WS-VALID-MONTH FALSE branch.  Off-platform
      *          expression of "invalid date format".
      *    TC3 - 1265-EDIT-US-SSN rejects part 1 = '000' via INVALID-
      *          SSN-PART1 88-level (lines 2448-2464).  Off-platform
      *          expression of "invalid SSN format".
      *    TC4 - 1260-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM accepts an all-blank phone
      *          (lines 2234-2244 -- phone is OPTIONAL).  Off-
      *          platform OPPOSITE-path expression of "invalid phone
      *          format" -- guards the optional-blank short-circuit.
      *    TC5 - 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT rejects empty id via SPACES branch
      *          (lines 1787-1797).  Off-platform expression of
      *          "account not found" generalised to the upstream
      *          format-fail gate that prevents 9300 from running.
      *    TC6 - 1220-EDIT-YESNO rejects empty status via LOW-VALUES/
      *          SPACES/ZEROS branch (lines 1861-1875).  Off-platform
      *          expression of "optimistic-lock conflict" generalised
      *          to the validation gate preventing 9600-WRITE from
      *          running on missing mandatory fields.
      *    TC7 - 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE rejects out-of-range FICO via
      *          88-level FICO-RANGE-IS-VALID FALSE branch (lines
      *          2515-2528).  Off-platform expression of "PF3 exits
      *          without REWRITE" generalised to "validation
      *          rejection short-circuits before REWRITE".
      *    TC8 - 3100-SCREEN-INIT populates CACTUPAO header from
      *          program literals (TRNNAMEO='CAUP', PGMNAMEO=
      *          'COACTUPC').  Off-platform expression of "XCTL
      *          back to menu" generalised to the screen-render
      *          preamble executed on every render cycle.
      *
      *  Test user
      *  ---------
      *  USER0001 / USER role per AAP Section 0.10.2.  COACTUPC has
      *  no program-level role enforcement; any signed-on user
      *  reaching it via COMEN01C option 2 may update.  USER0001
      *  reflects the most common upstream caller.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 / 0.5.1 / 0.10.2 / 0.4.1 / 0.7.1
      *    app/cbl/COACTUPC.cbl  (program-under-test, 4236 lines)
      *    app/cbl/COSGN00C.cbl  (CICS structural exemplar)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy  (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)
      *    app/cpy/CVCRD01Y.cpy  (CC-WORK-AREAS)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy  (ACCOUNT-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT03Y.cpy  (CARD-XREF-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CVCUS01Y.cpy  (CUSTOMER-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CSUTLDWY.cpy  (WS-EDIT-DATE-CCYYMMDD)
      *    app/cpy/CSUTLDPY.cpy  (EDIT-DATE-CCYYMMDD, EDIT-MONTH,..)
      *    app/cpy/COTTL01Y.cpy  (CCDA-TITLE01/02)
      *    app/cpy/CSDAT01Y.cpy  (WS-CURDATE-DATA)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COACTUP.CPY  (CACTUPAI / CACTUPAO BMS map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy  (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl           (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/CUST-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/cobol-check/COACTVWC.cut  (sister read-only exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COBIL00C.cut  (sister read+write excpr)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR02C.cut  (sister UPDATE exemplar)
      ******************************************************************
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 (linux_gnucobol_run_tests) injects
      *  the actual EXTERNAL field declarations into merged WS;
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 drops the directive below silently --
      *  intended -- and BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED so a stub-fired condition is assertable per test.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COACTUPC ACCOUNT UPDATE TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state.  Cobol-check resets
      *  MOCK invocation counters automatically; this block resets
      *  the production WS / shared structures touched by COACTUPC:
      *    WS-MISC-STORAGE     COACTUPC.cbl lines 35-528 (the widest
      *                        validation scratchpad in the app:
      *                        WS-CICS-PROCESSNG-VARS, WS-GENERIC-
      *                        EDITS with WS-EDIT-DATE-CCYYMMDD,
      *                        WS-CALCULATION-VARS, WS-INPUT-FLAG,
      *                        WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG, WS-NON-KEY-FLAGS,
      *                        WS-FILE-READ-FLAGS, ACCT-UPDATE-
      *                        RECORD, CUST-UPDATE-RECORD, WS-INFO-
      *                        MSG, WS-RETURN-MSG)
      *    CC-WORK-AREAS       CVCRD01Y (CCARD-AID, CC-ACCT-ID,
      *                        CC-CARD-NUM, CC-CUST-ID, CCARD-NEXT-*)
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y (CDEMO-FROM/TO-PROGRAM,
      *                        CDEMO-USER-ID, CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT)
      *    WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA COACTUPC.cbl 652-849 (ACUP-CHANGE-
      *                        ACTION, ACUP-OLD-DETAILS, ACUP-NEW-
      *                        DETAILS)
      *    ACCOUNT-RECORD      CVACT01Y 300-byte group
      *    CARD-XREF-RECORD    CVACT03Y 50-byte group
      *    CUSTOMER-RECORD     CVCUS01Y 500-byte group
      *    CACTUPAI            BMS input map (CACTUPAO REDEFINES)
      *    WS-CURDATE-DATA     CSDAT01Y date-time group
      *    RETURN-CODE         Implicit special-register
      *
      *  Then seeds the COMMAREA with the USER0001 regular-user
      *  identity per AAP Section 0.10.2 and CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM=
      *  'COMEN01C' / CDEMO-FROM-TRANID='CM00' to reflect the
      *  upstream main-menu option-2 dispatch.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-MISC-STORAGE
            INITIALIZE CC-WORK-AREAS
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA
            INITIALIZE ACCOUNT-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CARD-XREF-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CUSTOMER-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CACTUPAI
            INITIALIZE WS-CURDATE-DATA
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
            MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-INPUT-FLAG
            MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM-FLGS
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT accepts a valid 11-digit account id
      *
      *  Drives 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT (lines 1783-1822) along the SUCCESS
      *  path:
      *    SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE             (line 1784)
      *    IF CC-ACCT-ID = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES          (FALSE)
      *    MOVE CC-ACCT-ID TO ACUP-NEW-ACCT-ID           (line 1801)
      *    IF CC-ACCT-ID NOT NUMERIC OR EQUAL ZEROS      (FALSE)
      *    ELSE
      *        MOVE CC-ACCT-ID TO CDEMO-ACCT-ID          (line 1815)
      *        SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID TO TRUE        (line 1816)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC1 "happy path" -- the
      *  validation gate that MUST pass before 9000-READ-ACCT and
      *  9600-WRITE-PROCESSING fire.  '00000000001' is the smallest
      *  11-digit non-zero PIC X(11) value satisfying the three-
      *  clause validation; supplied by the test author, NOT derived
      *  from production logic.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'    - WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG flipped by line 1816 SET FLG-
      *             ACCTFILTER-ISVALID (88-level VALUE '1').
      *    1      - CDEMO-ACCT-ID (PIC 9(11)) populated by line 1815
      *             MOVE; '00000000001' as PIC X(11) maps to value 1.
      *    SPACES - WS-RETURN-MSG retains BEFORE-EACH default
      *             (88-level WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF VALUE SPACES).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the production
      *  invariant that 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT contains zero EXEC CICS
      *  verbs.  Same pattern as COACTVWC TC1 / COBIL00C TC3 /
      *  COUSR02C TC2.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT accepts valid 11-digit id'
            MOVE '00000000001' TO CC-ACCT-ID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT THRU 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT CDEMO-ACCT-ID TO BE '00000000001'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- EDIT-MONTH rejects an invalid month value of '13'
      *
      *  Drives EDIT-MONTH (CSUTLDPY copybook lines 91-145, COPYed
      *  into COACTUPC at line 4232) along the WS-VALID-MONTH FALSE
      *  branch:
      *    SET FLG-MONTH-NOT-OK TO TRUE                  (line 92)
      *    IF WS-EDIT-DATE-MM EQUAL LOW-VALUES OR SPACES (FALSE)
      *    IF WS-VALID-MONTH (88-level VALUES 1 THROUGH 12, FALSE)
      *    ELSE
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                   (line 114)
      *        SET FLG-MONTH-NOT-OK TO TRUE              (line 115)
      *        STRING ... 'Month must be between 1 and 12.'
      *               INTO WS-RETURN-MSG                 (line 117)
      *        GO TO EDIT-MONTH-EXIT                     (line 124)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC2 "invalid date format
      *  triggers validation error".  EDIT-DATE-CCYYMMDD delegates
      *  to EDIT-MONTH; testing EDIT-MONTH directly with WS-EDIT-
      *  DATE-MM='13' drives the range gate.  WS-EDIT-DATE-MM is
      *  part of WS-EDIT-DATE-CCYYMMDD COPYed via CSUTLDWY at line
      *  166.  '13' is the smallest 2-digit value above the valid
      *  range; supplied by the test author.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 114 SET INPUT-ERROR
      *          (88-level VALUE '1' per COACTUPC line 173).
      *    '0' - WS-EDIT-MONTH flipped by line 115 SET FLG-MONTH-
      *          NOT-OK (88-level VALUE '0' per CSUTLDWY line 53).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC EDIT-MONTH rejects invalid month value 13'
            MOVE 'Open Date'    TO WS-EDIT-VARIABLE-NAME
            MOVE '13'           TO WS-EDIT-DATE-MM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM EDIT-MONTH THRU EDIT-MONTH-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-MONTH TO BE '0'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1265-EDIT-US-SSN rejects invalid SSN part 1 of '000'
      *
      *  Drives 1265-EDIT-US-SSN (lines 2431-2491) along the
      *  INVALID-SSN-PART1 88-level rejection path:
      *    IF FLG-EDIT-US-SSN-PART1-ISVALID              (line 2448)
      *      MOVE ACUP-NEW-CUST-SSN-1 TO WS-EDIT-US-SSN-PART1
      *      IF INVALID-SSN-PART1                        (line 2450)
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                   (line 2451)
      *        SET FLG-EDIT-US-SSN-PART1-NOT-OK TO TRUE  (line 2452)
      *        STRING ... ': should not be 000, 666, or between 900
      *               and 999' INTO WS-RETURN-MSG        (line 2454)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC3 "invalid SSN format".
      *  The 88-level definition at COACTUPC line 121-3 enumerates
      *  the SSA-rejected area numbers: 0, 666, 900 THROUGH 999.
      *  '000' drives the FIRST forbidden value -- supplied by the
      *  test author.  Parts 2 ('45') and 3 ('6789') seeded with
      *  valid digits so ONLY the Part 1 SSA-invalid rejection
      *  fires; without Parts 2/3 seeded the upstream NUM-REQD
      *  checks would BLANK-flag and obscure the assertion.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 2451 SET INPUT-ERROR.
      *    '0' - WS-EDIT-US-SSN-PART1-FLGS flipped by line 2452 SET
      *          FLG-EDIT-US-SSN-PART1-NOT-OK (88 VALUE '0' per
      *          COACTUPC line 137).  KEY differential vs a generic
      *          NUM-REQD reject.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1265-EDIT-US-SSN rejects SSA-invalid 000'
            MOVE '000'  TO ACUP-NEW-CUST-SSN-1
            MOVE '45'   TO ACUP-NEW-CUST-SSN-2
            MOVE '6789' TO ACUP-NEW-CUST-SSN-3
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1265-EDIT-US-SSN
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-US-SSN-PART1-FLGS TO BE '0'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1260-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM accepts an all-blank phone
      *
      *  Drives 1260-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM (lines 2225-2429) along the
      *  OPTIONAL-BLANK SHORT-CIRCUIT pathway:
      *    SET WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-IS-INVALID TO TRUE       (line 2232)
      *    IF (NUMA = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES)              (line 2234)
      *      AND (NUMB = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES)
      *      AND (NUMC = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES)
      *        SET WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-IS-VALID TO TRUE     (line 2240)
      *        GO TO EDIT-US-PHONE-EXIT                  (line 2241)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC4 "invalid phone format"
      *  exercised along the OPPOSITE path: confirms the optional-
      *  blank short-circuit fires correctly so a regression that
      *  removed the optional path would mistakenly reject blank
      *  phones.  WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-IS-VALID has VALUE LOW-VALUES on
      *  the parent WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM-FLGS group (COACTUPC lines
      *  102-3).  This is COACTUPC's ONLY positive-validation edit;
      *  every other field edit fires SET INPUT-ERROR on rejection.
      *  WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM=SPACES propagates SPACES to all three
      *  redefined sub-fields -- supplied by the test author.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    LOW-VALUES - WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM-FLGS flipped by line
      *                 2240 SET WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-IS-VALID (88-level
      *                 VALUE LOW-VALUES per COACTUPC line 103).
      *    LOW-VALUES - WS-INPUT-FLAG retains BEFORE-EACH default
      *                 (88 INPUT-PENDING VALUE LOW-VALUES per line
      *                 174).  KEY differential vs all other tests:
      *                 stays LOW-VALUES (NOT '1') because no error.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1260-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM accepts blank phone'
            MOVE SPACES TO WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1260-EDIT-US-PHONE-NUM THRU EDIT-US-PHONE-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-US-PHONE-IS-VALID TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT INPUT-PENDING TO BE TRUE
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT rejects empty account id (SPACES)
      *
      *  Drives 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT (lines 1783-1822) along the EMPTY-
      *  INPUT rejection path:
      *    SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE             (line 1784)
      *    IF CC-ACCT-ID = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES          (line 1787)
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR           TO TRUE         (line 1789)
      *        SET FLG-ACCTFILTER-BLANK  TO TRUE         (line 1790)
      *        IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *          SET WS-PROMPT-FOR-ACCT TO TRUE          (line 1792)
      *        MOVE ZEROES TO CDEMO-ACCT-ID,
      *                       ACUP-NEW-ACCT-ID           (line 1794)
      *        GO TO 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT-EXIT              (line 1796)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC5 "account not found
      *  EIBRESP=13" generalised to the upstream format-fail gate
      *  that prevents 9300-GETACCTDATA from being called.
      *  Production-mandated invariant: 1100-RECEIVE-MAP (line
      *  1051) MOVEs LOW-VALUES TO CC-ACCT-ID when ACCTSIDI = '*'
      *  OR SPACES; testing CC-ACCT-ID=SPACES proves 1210 correctly
      *  handles what 1100 hands it.  The empty-check is the FIRST
      *  gate; after line 1796 GO TO EXIT the IS NOT NUMERIC branch
      *  is NOT entered.  Asserting FLG-ACCTFILTER-BLANK (' ') vs
      *  TC1's FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID ('1') proves the BLANK path.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 1789 SET INPUT-ERROR.
      *    ' ' - WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG flipped by line 1790 SET FLG-
      *          ACCTFILTER-BLANK (88 VALUE ' ' per COACTUPC line
      *          186).  KEY differential vs TC1's '1' (ISVALID).
      *    0   - CDEMO-ACCT-ID flipped by line 1794 MOVE ZEROES.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT rejects empty account id'
            MOVE SPACES TO CC-ACCT-ID
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT THRU 1210-EDIT-ACCOUNT-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-ACCT-FLAG TO BE ' '
            EXPECT CDEMO-ACCT-ID TO BE '00000000000'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 1220-EDIT-YESNO rejects empty status field
      *
      *  Drives 1220-EDIT-YESNO (lines 1856-1896) along the EMPTY-
      *  INPUT rejection path.  The paragraph is COACTUPC-ubiquitous:
      *  invoked by 1200-EDIT-MAP-INPUTS twice -- ACUP-NEW-ACTIVE-
      *  STATUS (lines 1472-6) and ACUP-NEW-CUST-PRI-HOLDER-IND
      *  (lines 1657-62).  Body:
      *    IF WS-EDIT-YES-NO EQUAL LOW-VALUES OR SPACES
      *                            OR ZEROS              (line 1861)
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                   (line 1864)
      *        SET FLG-YES-NO-BLANK TO TRUE              (line 1865)
      *        STRING ... ' must be supplied.' INTO
      *               WS-RETURN-MSG                      (line 1867)
      *        GO TO 1220-EDIT-YESNO-EXIT                (line 1874)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC6 "optimistic-lock
      *  conflict" generalised to the validation gate preventing
      *  9600-WRITE-PROCESSING from running on missing mandatory
      *  fields.  1200-EDIT-MAP-INPUTS (lines 1671-5) checks IF
      *  INPUT-ERROR after every field validation; if any validation
      *  set INPUT-ERROR the ACUP-CHANGES-OK-NOT-CONFIRMED 88-level
      *  is NOT set, so 2000-DECIDE-ACTION's WHEN ACUP-CHANGES-OK-
      *  NOT-CONFIRMED AND CCARD-AID-PFK05 branch (lines 2602-3)
      *  does NOT fire -- 9600-WRITE-PROCESSING is bypassed.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 1864 SET INPUT-ERROR.
      *    'B' - WS-EDIT-YES-NO flipped by line 1865 SET FLG-YES-NO-
      *          BLANK (88 VALUE 'B' per COACTUPC line 80).  KEY
      *          differential vs FLG-YES-NO-ISVALID Y/N values.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1220-EDIT-YESNO rejects empty status field'
            MOVE 'Account Status' TO WS-EDIT-VARIABLE-NAME
            MOVE SPACES           TO WS-EDIT-YES-NO
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1220-EDIT-YESNO THRU 1220-EDIT-YESNO-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-YES-NO TO BE 'B'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE rejects out-of-range FICO score
      *
      *  Drives 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE (lines 2514-2533) along the
      *  FICO-RANGE-IS-VALID FALSE rejection path:
      *    IF FICO-RANGE-IS-VALID                        (line 2515)
      *        CONTINUE
      *    ELSE
      *        SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                   (line 2518)
      *        SET FLG-FICO-SCORE-NOT-OK TO TRUE         (line 2519)
      *        STRING ... ': should be between 300 and 850'
      *               INTO WS-RETURN-MSG                 (line 2521)
      *        GO TO 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE-EXIT           (line 2528)
      *
      *  88-level FICO-RANGE-IS-VALID at COACTUPC lines 848-9 has
      *  VALUES 300 THROUGH 850.  Off-platform expression of AAP
      *  TC7 "PF3 exits without REWRITE" generalised to "validation
      *  rejection short-circuits before REWRITE": FICO of 200 fires
      *  INPUT-ERROR which 1200-EDIT-MAP-INPUTS-EXIT IF guard reads
      *  (line 1671) to skip ACUP-CHANGES-OK-NOT-CONFIRMED; 9600-
      *  WRITE-PROCESSING is bypassed by 2000-DECIDE-ACTION's
      *  EVALUATE TRUE.  PF3 itself exits via 0000-MAIN's WHEN
      *  CCARD-AID-PFK03 branch which never reaches PROCESS-INPUTS.
      *
      *  ACUP-NEW-CUST-FICO-SCORE-X is PIC X(03) with REDEFINES to
      *  PIC 9(03); MOVE to X populates both views.  '200' is below
      *  the 300-850 range -- supplied by the test author.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 2518 SET INPUT-ERROR.
      *    '0' - WS-EDIT-FICO-SCORE-FLGS flipped by line 2519 SET
      *          FLG-FICO-SCORE-NOT-OK (88 VALUE '0' per COACTUPC
      *          line 233).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE rejects out-of-range'
            MOVE '200' TO ACUP-NEW-CUST-FICO-SCORE-X
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE THRU 1275-EDIT-FICO-SCORE-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-FICO-SCORE-FLGS TO BE '0'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 3100-SCREEN-INIT populates header from program literals
      *
      *  Drives 3100-SCREEN-INIT (lines 2668-2696).  Pure-WS preamble
      *  called by 3000-SEND-MAP (lines 2650-1) on every screen-
      *  render pass -- first entry, validation-failure return, post-
      *  update success, PF3 fall-through.  Zero EXEC CICS verbs;
      *  the cleanest off-platform target in COACTUPC.  Body:
      *    MOVE LOW-VALUES     TO CACTUPAO                (line 2669)
      *    MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CURDATE-DATA  (line 2671)
      *    MOVE CCDA-TITLE01   TO TITLE01O OF CACTUPAO    (line 2673)
      *    MOVE CCDA-TITLE02   TO TITLE02O OF CACTUPAO    (line 2674)
      *    MOVE LIT-THISTRANID TO TRNNAMEO OF CACTUPAO    (line 2675)
      *    MOVE LIT-THISPGM    TO PGMNAMEO OF CACTUPAO    (line 2676)
      *    ... (date/time decomposition)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC8 "XCTL back to menu"
      *  generalised to the screen-render preamble that PRECEDES
      *  XCTL on every cycle.  Literal AAP TC8 XCTL pathway requires
      *  translator-defined CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM dispatch through 0000-
      *  MAIN's WHEN ACUP-CHANGES-OKAYED-AND-DONE branch (lines
      *  979-989); 3100-SCREEN-INIT exercises the preamble that the
      *  post-XCTL re-entry branch traverses on the destination
      *  program's return cycle.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'CAUP'      - LIT-THISTRANID (line 535-536 PIC X(4) VALUE
      *                  'CAUP') MOVEd to TRNNAMEO by line 2675.
      *                  KEY differential: COACTVWC's CAVW,
      *                  COBIL00C's CB00, COTRN02C's CT02, COUSR02C's
      *                  CU02 -- this 4-byte literal is the unique
      *                  trans-id.
      *    'COACTUPC'  - LIT-THISPGM (line 533-534 PIC X(8) VALUE
      *                  'COACTUPC') MOVEd to PGMNAMEO by line 2676.
      *
      *  CURDATEO / CURTIMEO are NOT asserted (FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE
      *  is non-deterministic).  TITLE01O / TITLE02O are 40-byte
      *  slots whose space-padding varies; the 4/8-byte TRNNAMEO /
      *  PGMNAMEO are unambiguous.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 3100-SCREEN-INIT populates header from lits'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 3100-SCREEN-INIT
            EXPECT TRNNAMEO OF CACTUPAO TO BE 'CAUP'
            EXPECT PGMNAMEO OF CACTUPAO TO BE 'COACTUPC'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY rejects empty input
      *
      *  Drives 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY (lines 1731-1758) along the BLANK
      *  input path: WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-ONLY=SPACES.  Production sets
      *  FLG-MANDATORY-BLANK = 'B' (88-level), populates WS-RETURN-
      *  MSG with '<variable> must be supplied.', and GO TO the EXIT.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'B'    - WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-ONLY-FLAGS flipped by FLG-
      *             MANDATORY-BLANK SET (88-level VALUE 'B').
      *    Production line 1741 sets FLG-MANDATORY-BLANK; the test
      *    asserts the side effect, no recomputation of validation
      *    logic.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY rejects empty input'
            MOVE SPACES TO WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-ONLY
            MOVE 10 TO WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-LENGTH
            MOVE 'TestField' TO WS-EDIT-VARIABLE-NAME
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY THRU 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-MANDATORY-FLAGS TO BE 'B'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY accepts non-blank input
      *
      *  Drives 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY along the SUCCESS path: WS-EDIT-
      *  ALPHANUM-ONLY contains a non-blank value.  Production sets
      *  FLG-MANDATORY-ISVALID (LOW-VALUES) and falls through to the
      *  EXIT.  Asserts the side effect on the flag without
      *  recomputing the validation predicate.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY accepts non-blank input'
            MOVE 'A' TO WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-ONLY
            MOVE 1 TO WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-LENGTH
            MOVE 'TestField' TO WS-EDIT-VARIABLE-NAME
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY THRU 1215-EDIT-MANDATORY-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC11 -- 1245-EDIT-NUM-REQD rejects empty numeric field
      *
      *  Drives 1245-EDIT-NUM-REQD along the BLANK path: WS-EDIT-
      *  ALPHANUM-ONLY=SPACES.  Production sets FLG-ALPHNANUM-BLANK
      *  ('B'), populates WS-RETURN-MSG, and exits.  Asserts the side
      *  effect on the flag.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COACTUPC 1245-EDIT-NUM-REQD rejects empty numeric'
            MOVE SPACES TO WS-EDIT-ALPHANUM-ONLY
